================================================================================
DECENTRALIZED FREELANCE ESCROW SYSTEM - BACKEND IMPLEMENTATION PLAN
================================================================================

This plan outlines the architecture, tech stack, and directory layout for building
the backend of our decentralized, secure, and trustless freelance escrow system.
As instructed, we are using the existing folder layout and will not create new folders.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. THE TECH STACK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Runtime: Node.js
* Web Framework: Express.js (fast, unopinionated, lightweight for microservices)
* Database: MongoDB + Mongoose (perfect for storing off-chain metadata, user ratings,
  negotiated terms, and blockchain event logs)
* Web3 Libraries:
  - Ethers.js (v6) - To interact with the smart contract, sign messages, and recover 
    signatures for secure logins.
* Authentication:
  - JWT (JSON Web Tokens) paired with Web3 Wallet Signature-based authentication.
    Users will log in securely using their cryptographic keys (e.g. MetaMask).

